<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Young Khivans</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1910s–1920s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Young Khivans were a reformist movement in the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a>, formed in the 1910s on the model of the Young Turks and the Jadid reformers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. In 1920, allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>, they overthrew the last khan, Said Abdullah, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junaid-khan">Junaid Khan</a>, and led the new Khorezm People's Soviet Republic until communists displaced them.</p></div>
